  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5321",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a complex relationship with TERT-RPE1 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for A704, which in turn is targeted by palmarumycin CP18 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, both of which ultimately target TERT-RPE1. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Mollicellin N may influence the biological activity of these compounds, potentially through the modulation of A704 or other downstream targets. The overlapping targets between different compounds, such as A704 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, suggest a possible functional relationship or shared regulatory mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mollicellin N to play a role in the biological processes that lead to TERT-RPE1 activation, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
